+# Bridge → Hermes source mapping
+
+Baseline: installed checkout /Users/dippo/.hermes/hermes-agent, HEAD 2a4c9afd7bd7b56d3e1f95524ca8956092f2904c. Hermes is an upstream dependency. This implementation changes no Hermes source, provider runtime, agent loop, scheduler, tool policy, profile files or production databases.
+
+See [MOBILE_CAPABILITY_MAP.md](MOBILE_CAPABILITY_MAP.md) and [MOBILE_ARCHITECTURE.md](MOBILE_ARCHITECTURE.md) for the completed source audit. The actual implemented contract is [BRIDGE_API.md](BRIDGE_API.md).
+
+Abbreviations below: DS = hermes_cli/web_server.py; RPC = tui_gateway/server.py; KB = plugins/kanban/dashboard/plugin_api.py. Line numbers refer to the audited commit. All Studio-side implementation is in hermes-mobile-bridge/src/hermes_mobile_bridge.
+
+| Bridge operation | Hermes mechanism and source | Normalization / limits |
+|---|---|---|
+| Connection/health | DS:11507 /api/ws; tui_gateway/ws.py handles structured frames; RPC:4878 session.active_list | One reconnecting socket per explicitly configured profile backend. Phone suspension never closes this socket. Heartbeat and bounded backoff; independent local REST client. |
+| Upstream authentication | DS:216 session token; DS:11071 WS gate; DS:11507 upgrade | Deliberately provisioned loopback session token; Studio-only bearer REST and local query-token WS. No scraping or server-internal credential impersonation. |
+| Capability discovery | Dashboard /openapi.json, successful session.active_list, configured allowlists; RPC:2601 desktop contract=2 | Dynamic route availability + current connection + bridge-local features. Not API-server jobs_admin flags. CLI can verify installed source HEAD; HTTP provides no binary attestation. |
+| Conversation list/search | DS:2842 /api/sessions; DS:3047 /api/sessions/search | Explicit profile, bounded limit/offset, opaque profile/session mapping, allowlisted metadata. Draft metadata can supplement an empty collection. |
+| Conversation inspect/history | DS:7311 detail; DS:7339 messages; hermes_state.py:2684 get_messages | Hermes remains transcript owner. Messages follows compression continuation. Bridge records aliases to maintain conversation identity across verified lineage rotation. |
+| Conversation creation | RPC:4183 session.create | Source=mobile, close_on_disconnect=false; model/provider/reasoning are per-session creation overrides. Empty drafts may not yet exist in Hermes's DB. |
+| Resume/ownership | RPC:4417 session.resume; RPC:4878 active_list | Existing handles matched to stored/live identity; reject known foreign/busy handle. Reconnect reattaches only the same previously owned executing handle. No automatic replacement execution. Other processes cannot be exhaustively enumerated. |
+| Rename/archive | DS:7386 PATCH session; profile is in body | Uses canonical DB metadata, not the legacy global-profile title RPC. No raw config. |
+| Delete | RPC:5731 session.close, RPC:4940 session.delete | Refuse bridge active/unknown work and known foreign live handles; close only an owned idle handle, then use guarded RPC deletion. Metadata/run observations remain. External-process write races cannot be globally ruled out. |
+| Start run | RPC:6097 prompt.submit | Bridge UUID observation persisted before dispatch; one unresolved run per conversation; command receipt before request. Hermes executes. Prompt is never automatically resent after reconnect/crash. |
+| Run status/list | RPC message.start, message.complete, error; active_list for reconciliation | Durable bridge run ID is not a Hermes global run ID. Missing handle/unknown outcome stays unknown. Goal continuation message.start creates a linked execution. Chat task_id=null. |
+| Assistant streaming | RPC:6491 streaming callback; RPC:6584 message.complete | Plain text deltas, replace-on-completion, nullable interruption text normalized to empty. ANSI rendered output omitted. Bounded journal survives phone disconnection. |
+| Tool events/results | RPC:2840 _on_tool_start; RPC:2867 _on_tool_complete | Allowlisted structured tool fields; no arbitrary event proxy. Failed result with error maps to tool.failed. Source tool-progress setting can suppress events; configured inventory is not effective live-tool health. |
+| Event replay | No upstream chat replay primitive; bridge store.py | SQLite global monotonic sequence/epoch, per-run/global retention floors, count/age/byte limits. Nondestructive multiple readers; old cursor fails visibly. Raw frames bounded/internal. |
+| Stop | RPC:5814 session.interrupt; run_agent.py:2376 interrupt; tools.approval.py:728 resolve_gateway_approval | Cooperative whole-run stop; acknowledgement is not termination. Persist stop intent; reassert interrupt for a late prompt that appears after the first FIFO clear. No per-approval response is dispatched. |
+| Steering | RPC:6060 session.steer; run_agent core queue | Queued versus rejected acknowledgement, no claimed consumed event. Local real-provider test verifies steering reaches a subsequent model request, but API still only guarantees queued semantics. |
+| Retry | New RPC prompt.submit after failed/cancelled observed execution | Explicit new bridge run and command ID; previous result is preserved. No retry of unknown outcomes or missing goal prompts. Tool effects can already exist: retry is a new execution, not rollback. |
+| Dangerous approvals | RPC approval.request; RPC:7589 approval.respond delegates FIFO resolution; tools/approval.py pending queues | Observe context and bind attention to bridge run/session. Always disable remote choices, including deny: upstream lacks compare-and-resolve exact targeting. Generated IDs do not fix this. |
+| Clarifications/local secrets | RPC:1459 _block creates request ID/default 300s; RPC:7556 _respond, clarify.respond/sudo.respond/secret.respond/terminal.read.respond | Exact clarifications only while same generation/pending/under 290s. Replayed ID never becomes fresh. Secret/sudo/terminal-buffer input stays local. Disconnect/completion marks uncertain; bridge expiry is not upstream resolution proof. |
+| Profiles/SOUL/activity | DS:9750 profiles; DS:9545 profile metadata; DS:10006 SOUL; DS:3416 model info; RPC active_list | Configured identity/description/model/provider/skill metadata/SOUL and observed backend activity. No first-class bots/groups/mentions invented. Canonical sessions are accessed through profile queries. |
+| Creation model/reasoning/workspace | RPC:4183 create overrides; hermes_constants.py:478 parser; RPC:4731 cwd setter exists | Mobile accepts configured workspace IDs at creation, no arbitrary path. Later reasoning writes are omitted because config.set reasoning persists global defaults. No raw model flag strings from phone. |
+| Cron list/detail/results | DS:7616/7634/7645 jobs/detail/runs; cron/jobs.py; canonical cron sessions | Profile-scoped routines and recent result sessions; last_status/error/delivery_error remain distinct. No synthetic bridge task scheduler or invented per-execution outcome. |
+| Cron create/edit/delete | DS:7691 POST jobs; DS:7736 PUT updates; DS:7783 DELETE | Allowlisted fields only. No arbitrary script/base URL/immutable ID mutation. Enable/disable must use dedicated actions so scheduling state stays consistent. |
+| Cron enable/disable/run-now | DS:7750 pause, DS:7761 resume, DS:7772 trigger | Trigger advances due time; healthy Hermes scheduler required. Not the Chronos /api/cron/fire JWT webhook, and no duplicated execution in bridge. |
+| Kanban list/detail | KB:378 board, KB:517 task detail, KB:1352 workers; hermes_cli/kanban_db.py | Source task state distinct from attempt outcome. done→display complete; dependency links/mobile IDs, diagnostics/block reasons/heartbeat/attempts retained. PID/claim internals omitted. |
+| Kanban create/update/delete | KB:597 create, KB:821 PATCH, KB:944 delete | Real Hermes transition guards decide legality. Configured workspace maps to dir, not invented repo kind. running/review are not offered as PATCH targets. Assignment sent separately; compound source mutations can partially commit. |
+| Kanban reclaim/reassign | KB:1563 reclaim, KB:1651 reassign; kanban_db.reclaim_task/reassign_task | Hermes owns worker signals, lease release and outcome. No raw PID or generic kill API. Target worker must be authorized. |
+| Kanban activity | KB:2379 /events WS reads durable task_events rows by integer since cursor | Separate Studio-side observer per explicitly configured board, durable cursor and dedup key; mobile sees one normalized task.activity feed. Phone never opens these sockets. |
+| Home | DS status/system stats/cron; KB board; RPC active_list; bridge owned-run/attention journal | Derived canonical snapshots plus explicit observation coverage. Host failure and Hermes failure are separate. Per-read timeout supplies partial coverage errors. Not universal agent visibility. |
+| Attach images/PDF/files | RPC:6957 image.attach_bytes; RPC:7018 pdf.attach; RPC:7280 file.attach | Bridge upload bound, filename/type/base64 validation, owned idle session. File references appended internally to next prompt; phone does not assemble @file host paths. |
+| Registered artifacts | Known returned upload paths; structured tool-result file/image/artifact paths inside configured roots | Descriptor-relative no-symlink opens; no traversal/hard links; identity/size/mtime checked. No use of generic dashboard filesystem browsing/download as passthrough. Other generated files can remain undiscoverable. |
+| Kanban attachments | KB:517 attachment ownership metadata; KB:762 scoped download | Verify attachment belongs to requested task/board, cap transfer, proxy binary. No phone-supplied host path. Canonical upstream confinement remains upstream responsibility. |
+| Live token usage | RPC:2488 _get_usage; RPC:5200 session.usage | Actual token/cache/reasoning/context counters and available Hermes estimate; label cumulative scope. Do not synthesize run deltas/cost/quotas. |
+| Profile usage analytics | DS /api/analytics/usage | Allowlisted daily/model/totals/skills. Provider/account billing mutations are excluded. |
+| Skills/tools/models/MCP/memory | DS:10214 skills, DS:10320 toolsets, DS:3521 model options, DS:8002 MCP summaries, /api/memory | Read-only display fields. Remove credentials/base URLs/MCP commands/env/auth. MCP selection is configuration, not an external health probe. Memory provider/byte counts only. |
+| Mobile auth/version | Bridge cli.py/core.py/store.py; no Hermes auth change | Per-device high-entropy hashed scoped/revocable credentials, private files, optional direct TLS or deliberate tailnet HTTPS proxy. Tailscale is an additional network boundary. |
+
+## Why the HTTP run API is not used
+
+gateway/platforms/api_server.py implements /v1/runs, but its shared queue can be consumed/destructively cleaned up by stream disconnects. A sweeper removes execution/stream/control state about 300 seconds after creation, including active work. Native run status also has process-local retention and different history/model behavior. Using it would make a reconnecting phone unreliable.
+
+The bridge selects the existing desktop RPC agent path instead. It therefore does not need to keep an HTTP run handle alive, drain destructive queues or defeat a timer. Its own run observation survives indefinitely; bounded event retention is independent of run age. Both simulated >300-second observations and upstream handle loss are tested. This is not a patch or replacement runtime.
+
+## Remaining limits
+
+- One Hermes live session has one transport owner. A desktop resume/activate can steal the bridge's event sink without an observable ownership token. The bridge rejects known foreign handles but cannot reliably detect same-handle transport theft. Exclusive backend use is an operational requirement; supported shared observation requires an upstream primitive.
+- Independent gateway/CLI/cron/worker processes do not all share a live-control registry. Readable transcripts and task records do not imply a control handle. Home/activity explicitly reports coverage.
+- No exact dangerous-approval target exists. Remote approval is deliberately unavailable; stopping the entire owned run is a separate authorized action. Clarification request IDs do not provide a universal approval API.
+- Unobserved outcomes are unknown. A backend restart can lose active execution/events; canonical text can recover persisted conversation content, not missing tool/approval events.
+- Existing cron scheduling/dispatch and Kanban state transitions must remain healthy. The bridge does not silently start another scheduler or dispatcher. Kanban's non-CAS dashboard transitions can race independent clients; source guard failures surface as conflicts, and compound writes may be partial.
+- Some tool progress is configuration-gated. Attachment discovery supports known structured paths, not every tool/provider/output convention. PDF conversion and some host metrics depend on upstream installed utilities.
+- Model capabilities/configured providers are metadata, not a successful paid-provider test. This implementation's real execution tests use a local mock model, never production API keys.
+- No Bot Mode registry, bot room/group orchestration, @bot mention routing, notification delivery, arbitrary settings, logs, unrestricted files or billing operations have been fabricated.
+
+The bridge itself adds only durable observations, command receipts, auth, reconnect/replay, projections and narrow normalization. Conversations, executions, cron routines, Kanban tasks/attempts, tools, memory, skills and provider state remain Hermes-owned.
